Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||02:10 PM||||I have a lot or respect for the ogre and the info in his cave - but I find it hard to accept that simply filling your tank till the gas reaches the cap would do something to the vapor canister that would ruin it - esp if it triggers a O2 sensor error then - rich from fuel in canister.<P>  If that were the case then the new fieros off the line would have been swamped with check engine lights and O2 error codes right from day one.<P>   Maybe if the pump nozzel is defective and doesnt shut off, that seems to be what he is saying, but then you are gonna get baptized in petro when the gas comes shooting out the filler tube and all over your pants.<P>   If it really is true that we should not put more than 8 gallons of gas in our 10 gallon tanks then we need to come up with a fix - a longer vapor tube to the canister with a goose neck in it - something. Loosing 50 or 60 miles off the range of your tank is a major defect.<P>  Not trying to take a cheap shot at Ogre here - are we misunderstanding the info? or is it only a problem if the gas nozzel is defective and doesnt click off.<P>  If it is a fiero design defect is there a correction we can make?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Alex4mula||05-30-2001||03:40 PM||||SteveJ; That's what I mean. When I reached the top (near 11 gal) the click was immediate.<P>84Bill; Yeah is good. I'm really satisfied with the swap regarding that. My 2.8 gave me about 20mpg but was in really bad shape.<P>Ken; I think Ogre's tip relates to filling over capacity, i.e. over 10 or 11.9 gls.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||04:01 PM||||yes but how do you overfill a gas tank?! it the fuel doenst come up to the end of the filler tube you dont know if its full or if the nozzel is very touchy.<P>  maybe I will do some tests on this with an almost full tank and a gas can - pull the vent line off the vapor canister and see what it takes to force fuel up it.<P>  My point is, I cant believe if you tell the guy at the gas station to fillerup, and he fills it right to the top of the pipe, that could ruin the vapor canister - that would be a serious design flaw cause it would happen all the time.<P>  if the nozzel is broke and the gas overflows the filler tube and comes out all over the side of the car, then ok maybe. Is that what you mean by overfilling it?||||reg||1
