Z||000015||RNGCRSH||05-30-2001||08:06 PM||||I had this problem, it did not happen in a Fiero but instead in a Dodge Dakota.<P>I was driving my fathers truck and it began to mis on several cylinders randomly. When we took it to a mechanic they could not figure the problem out, so they started to throw parts at the engine (very costly) what they eventualy found was charcoal granuals fron the vapor canistor were clogging up the fuel rails. upon further inspection they foun the vapor canistor and all hoses completely full of gas. <P>My father when asked said "he always tops of the gas tank", but not anymore<P>When at the pump, and you read the little sign that says "do not top off" ,It is not there just to keep you from spilling gas.||||reg||1
Z||000016||theogre||05-31-2001||03:41 PM||||Wether or not topping off by itself can damage the vapor can depends allot on the type of delivery nozel used. <P>Certain Vapor Recovery nozels, now required by law almost everywhere, can be trouble because they rather effectivly seal the tank opening.<P>Keep in mind that the vapor can is only slightly higher than the filler opening. The fuel level in the filler neck is the same as the level in the vent line. (Basic law of hydraulics, A free flow liquid will always seek an equal level.) It doesn't take much pressure to slosh liquid fuel into the canister.<P>Another issue is that a stuffed tank has no expansion room. The liquid fuel expands quite a bit as it warms after pumping. Remember the stuff is comming from underground tanks that are usally much cooler than the car. This can contribute to trashed canisters and fuel leaking. Even in cool weather there can be considerable heating of the fuel tank.<P>As for getting a gallon or 2 more than normall.... Sort of the same problem. Allot of nozels are picky about what position they are in a tank. My pinto was a real pain in the ___ to fill unless you knew just how to hold the nozel in the filler. If you just put it in and let it hang you'd have it cutting off every 2 seconds. My fiero and van dont seem to care most of the time. Its a combination of nozel design vs filler neck design. Some combinations just don't play well together.||||reg||1
